  "notes": "Rules-as-code legal workbench: each statute step is a card showing a monospace identifier, type tag (CALCULATION gray / CONDITION blue), evaluated value pill for the selected test household (red 'false' when failing), the expression in a mono gray well, a CFR citation chip, and ← in / → out dependency counts. Amendment-affected steps carry an amber left rule and amber tag; the amendment panel in the left sidebar uses a warm cream background with red dots for 'not cited'. Navy #1d3557 is reserved for primary buttons and selection outline. Hidden tabs include a dependency Graph (column layout with edges), Test households, Parameters, Sources, Revisions. Almost no shadows; structure from 1px borders and pale backgrounds."
